{#
  ============================================================================
  TEMPLATE: provider-as-requester-eu-lab_fsh.twig
  ============================================================================
  PURPOSE
    Generates TWO active FSH instances that model the requesting provider for
    a EU laboratory order:

      1. PractitionerRole  — the requester's role, linked to their organisation.
      2. Organization      — the organisation on behalf of which the request
                             is made.

    There is no Practitioner instance. A third block used to emit one; it was
    removed on 2026-09-11. See "Removed Practitioner block" below before
    reinstating it.

  PROFILE CONFORMANCE
    PractitionerRole : PractitionerRoleEu   (EU lab profile variant; not EuCore)
    Organization     : OrganizationEu       (EU lab profile variant; not EuCore)

  CONTEXT — EU Lab vs EPS
    This template targets the EU Laboratory Report context and therefore uses
    the `PractitionerRoleEu` / `OrganizationEu` profiles rather than the
    `*EuCore` profiles used by provider-as-primarycarephysician-eps_fsh.twig.
    The requester is the clinician who ordered the lab tests, not the physician
    responsible for the patient's overall care.

  setInstance() USE
    Only the PractitionerRole instance is registered via `setInstance()`:
      → "Instance-PractitionerRole-<requester.instancerole>"
    The Organization instance uses direct `{{ }}` interpolation and is NOT
    registered in the `twigit()` return array.

  ADDRESS VARIABLES — `provider.*` IS CORRECT HERE
    The Organisation's address sub-elements read `provider.*`, not
    `requester.*`. That is deliberate and it works: the caller passes
    `$pdat->provider` alongside `$requester`, and `$pdat->provider` is the
    primary-care FACILITY from getClosestProvider() — name, address, city,
    postcode, country. Run 2 confirms it: all 230 requesting Organizations
    carry an address.

    An earlier note here warned this "may produce empty address blocks". It
    does not. What it does produce is a naming trap, and the removed
    Practitioner block fell straight into it.

  REMOVED PRACTITIONER BLOCK
    Until 2026-09-11 this template ended with a third instance reading
    `provider.instanceprovider`, `provider.providernameprefix` and the other
    name fields.

    The old header claimed that block was commented out and produced no
    output, and described a two-segment comment construction keeping it
    suppressed. None of that was true: the opening comment tag closed before
    the `Instance:` line, so the block was live code and rendered into every
    file. (Deliberately not spelled out here — writing a closing comment tag
    inside a comment ends it, which is the same trap.)

    It rendered empty. Those `provider.*` fields are assigned in
    synderai-v7.php inside `if ($thisartifact === "EPS")`, so the LAB path
    never has them. The output was an instance literally named
    `Instance-Practitioner-` with every field an empty string — one per file,
    which SUSHI rejected as an invalid id once and as a duplicate name 518
    times in run 1 (520 errors, issue #108).

    BEFORE REINSTATING IT, two independent blockers:
      1. The LAB path supplies no requesting clinician. `$pdat->provider` is a
         facility, not a person. The EPS path enriches it with a nearest-
         practitioner lookup; the LAB path does not.
      2. bundle-lab-report-eu.fsh.twig has no `entry[practitioner]` slice for
         the requester — only for the laboratory
         (`laboratory.instancepractitioner`). A requester Practitioner would
         be unreferenced in the bundle even if populated.
    Neither the role nor the bundle referenced it, which is why removing it
    changes no reference anywhere.

    A requesting clinician is legitimate FHIR — `PractitionerRole.practitioner`
    is 0..1, so a role with only an organization is conformant, and so would a
    role with both. If the LAB path ever gains a named requester: emit the
    Practitioner, reference it from the role, AND add the bundle slice. All
    three, or none.

  NO HTML OUTPUT
    Both %%HEAD%% and %%HTML%% sections are intentionally left empty.
    Each active FSH instance carries only a minimal plain-text `text.div`.

  ORGANISATION IDENTIFIER
    The Organisation identifier is caller-supplied (`requester.orgidentifier`)
    under the HL7 Europe OID namespace (`HL7EUROPEEXAMPLESOID`). No UUID is
    generated for this identifier — it is a stable business id.

  CONTEXT VARIABLES
  ┌──────────────────────────────────┬──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Variable                         │ Type     │ Description                              │
  ├──────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ requester.instancerole           │ string   │ UUID / id for the PractitionerRole.      │
  │                                  │          │ Registered via setInstance().            │
  │ requester.instanceorg            │ string   │ UUID / id for the Organization.          │
  │ requester.orgidentifier          │ string   │ Business identifier value for the        │
  │                                  │          │ requesting Organisation (under            │
  │                                  │          │ HL7EUROPEEXAMPLESOID).                   │
  │ requester.orgname                │ string   │ Display name of the requesting           │
  │                                  │          │ organisation.                            │
  │ provider.address                 │ string?  │ Street address of the requesting         │
  │                                  │          │ FACILITY, not of a person. By design —   │
  │                                  │          │ see "Address variables" above.           │
  │ provider.city                    │ string?  │ City of the requesting facility.         │
  │ provider.postcode                │ string?  │ Postal code of the requesting facility.  │
  │ provider.country                 │ string?  │ Country of the requesting facility.      │
  └──────────────────────────────────┴──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘

  GLOBAL VARIABLES USED
    HL7EUROPEEXAMPLESOID — OID root for the Organisation identifier system URI.

  AUTHOR   KH
  SINCE    2025-09-07
  CHANGED  2026-09-11 — removed the Practitioner block (#108); corrected the
           header, which described that block as commented out when it was not
  ============================================================================
#}

%%FSH%% {# ── Section marker required by the FSH pre-processor ─────────────── #}

{#
  ── Instance 1: PractitionerRole ────────────────────────────────────────────
  The requester's role, linked to their organisation. No `practitioner`
  element: the LAB path has no requesting clinician, only a facility.
  PractitionerRole.practitioner is 0..1, so this is conformant.
  Registered via setInstance() — the only tracked instance in this template.
#}
Instance: {{ setInstance("Instance-PractitionerRole-" ~ requester.instancerole) }}
InstanceOf: PractitionerRoleEu
Title: "Practitioner Role (EPS) Requester"
Description: "Practitioner Role Requester"
Usage: #inline
* id = "{{ requester.instancerole }}"
* organization = Reference(urn:uuid:{{ requester.instanceorg }})
{# Minimal narrative — identifies the role by its id #}
* text.status = #generated
* text.div = """
<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
Provider Role Id: {{ requester.instancerole }}
</div>
"""

{#
  ── Instance 2: Organization ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The requesting organisation — the practice or department that placed the lab
  order. Identified by a caller-supplied business identifier (not a generated
  UUID) under the HL7 Europe OID namespace.
  Note: Instance id interpolated directly — NOT registered via setInstance().

  Address fields read `provider.*` by design — `$pdat->provider` is the
  requesting facility. See "Address variables" in the file header.
#}
Instance: Instance-Organization-{{ requester.instanceorg }}
InstanceOf: OrganizationEu
Title: "Organization Requester"
Description: "Organization Requester"
Usage: #inline
* id = "{{ requester.instanceorg }}"

{# Business identifier under the HL7 Europe OID namespace #}
* identifier.system = "urn:oid:{{ HL7EUROPEEXAMPLESOID }}"
* identifier.value = "{{ requester.orgidentifier }}"
* identifier.assigner.display = "HL7 Europe"

* name = "{{ requester.orgname }}"

{# Address comes from $pdat->provider, the requesting facility #}
{% if provider.address is not empty %}
* address.line = "{{ provider.address }}"
{% endif %}
{% if provider.city is not empty %}
* address.city = "{{ provider.city }}"
{% endif %}
{% if provider.postcode is not empty %}
* address.postalCode = "{{ provider.postcode }}"
{% endif %}
{% if provider.country is not empty %}
* address.country = "{{ provider.country }}"
{% endif %}

{# Minimal narrative — shows the requesting organisation name #}
* text.status = #generated
* text.div = """
<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
Provider Organization: {{ requester.orgname }}
</div>
"""

{#
  ── No third instance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  A Practitioner block stood here until 2026-09-11 and rendered empty into
  every file. See "Removed Practitioner block" in the file header for why it
  is gone and what would have to change before one belongs here again.
#}

%%HEAD%% {# ── Section marker required by the FSH pre-processor ─────────────── #}
{# No HEAD output — this template produces no HTML table. #}

%%HTML%% {# ── Section marker required by the FSH pre-processor ─────────────── #}
{# No HTML output — this template produces no HTML table. #}
